        "topic": "Accounting Equation",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2006",
        "question_text": "<p>If assets are \u20b550,000 and liabilities are \u20b520,000, what is the owner's equity?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The accounting equation is: <b>Assets = Liabilities + Owner's Equity</b>. Rearranged, <b>Owner's Equity = Assets - Liabilities</b>. Thus, \u20b550,000 - \u20b520,000 = <b>\u20b530,000</b>.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
